title: Ref value seeds
tags: [[Customising the GUI]]
kind: reference
aliases: ref-seeds seed-rule ref-completion naming-references
summary: A [ref-seeds] rule says, per field, which metarecords a ref may point to and by which columns they are named — in completions, in typed values and where the value is shown.

A `ref` value is the uuid of a metarecord: unreadable, and impossible to type. A
''seed rule'' gives the targets of a field a name instead. It is used wherever the
field's value is entered or shown in the detail of a metarecord: the candidates of
its completion, what a typed value must spell, the line under a value, the text an
edit starts from, and the query the [[Value picker]] opens on.

!! The rule

Rules are in `gui/config.toml` ([[GUI configuration]]), one per field name:

```
[ref-seeds]
tag    = ['mf_schema = "tag"', 'path:path']
author = ['mf_schema = "person"', 'full_name name']
'*'    = 'path:path mfr_path:path name label'
```

A rule is `["query", "columns"]`, or `"columns"` alone:

* the ''query'' says which metarecords may be named, in the query language; without one, all of them;
* the ''columns'' say how each is named, in the syntax of the columns of the metarecord list — `path:path` is the full path of a `tree_ref` field, `author>name` follows a reference.

`*` is the rule of every field that has none. A rule with more than two parts stops
the GUI at startup.

The shipped file names the three fields of the tag model (`tag`, `negative_tag`,
`mixed_tag`) by the path of the tag ([[Hierarchical tags]]), and everything else, by
`*`, by a path, a name or a label.

!! Typing a value

The value is typed as the target's ''label'': its columns, joined by the separator
of `[completion]` (`label-separator`, `" | "` when not set). A column the target
does not have is left out.

* The label is matched ''whole''. A text that names no candidate is an error, and so is a label that several targets bear — the error lists them. A wrong reference is never written silently.
* A uuid (32 hexadecimal characters) is always accepted as it is.

!! The candidates

The completion offers the naming as several views ([[Completion views]]): the whole
line first, then each column alone — a column's view listing only the metarecords
that have that column. Which one reaches a metarecord fastest depends on the
metarecord.

Each view is one page of at most 100 candidates, sorted by the naming columns and
asked of the daemon again as the text changes: every word typed must appear in one
of the columns. A rule may therefore select the whole repository.

While a view is on screen, a text names what it names ''in that view''. A value
given with the command, with no view to read it in, is looked up in all of them and
must name one target across them.

!! Reading a value back

What is typed is what is shown: under a `ref` value, and as the starting text of an
edit, the target reads as its label under the same rule. A target that has none of
the columns reads as its uuid, in the candidates as well.

!! Older tables

Two tables that came before `[ref-seeds]` are still read for a field that no rule
covers, which requires that there be no `*` rule either: `[picker-seeds]` (field →
the query the value picker opens on) and `[ref-completion-seeds]` (field → a
`tree_ref` field whose paths name the targets).
